{"question": "What space-specific constraints make CWE-200 (Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor) more dangerous in satellite operations?", "answer": "CWE-200 is more dangerous in satellite operations due to the inability to physically access the spacecraft for patching, the extreme latency in communication that delays response to exposures, and the resource constraints of radiation-hardened processors that limit the implementation of robust encryption and data sanitization measures. Additionally, the RF attack surface of the link segment increases the risk of interception by adversaries.", "citations": ["Information exposures can occur in different ways:

                  the code explicitly inserts sensitive information into resources or messages that are intentionally made accessible to unauthorized actors, but should not contain the information - i.e., the information should have been "scrubbed" or "sanitized"
                  a different weakness or mistake indirectly inserts the sensitive information into resources, such as a web script error revealing the full system path"], "grounding_score": 0.717}

{"question": "How does the Develop/Obtain Capabilities: DSSS or Frequency hopping sequence (ESA-T2007.004) control enhance the Least Functionality | Authorized Software (CM-7(5)) technique in satellite communication systems?", "answer": "The Develop/Obtain Capabilities: DSSS or Frequency hopping sequence (ESA-T2007.004) control enhances the Least Functionality | Authorized Software (CM-7(5)) technique by ensuring that only authorized frequency hopping sequences or DSSS codes are used in satellite communications. This aligns with the deny-all, permit-by-exception policy of CM-7(5), as it restricts the communication protocols to pre-authorized sequences, thereby preventing unauthorized or malicious software from exploiting the communication link.", "citations": ["CM-7(5): Authorized Software – Allow-by-exception
Control Statement
- Identify [Assignment: organization-defined software programs];
- Employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs on the system; and
- Review and update the list of authorized software programs [Assignment: organization-defined frequency]."], "grounding_score": 0.765999972820282}
